Risk Management Plan – Cybersecurity Project

I developed a comprehensive Risk Management Plan for Health Network, Inc., a fictional healthcare organization that manages sensitive medical and financial information. The project focused on identifying cybersecurity risks, evaluating their likelihood and impact, and recommending security controls to reduce those risks.

I used the NIST Cybersecurity Framework and NIST SP 800-53 to structure the plan around the Govern, Identify, Protect, Detect, Respond, and Recover functions. I analyzed threats including ransomware, phishing, DDoS attacks, insider threats, data loss, zero-day exploits, unsecured mobile devices, and physical security breaches. Each risk was evaluated based on likelihood and potential business impact.

The project also mapped risks to specific NIST security controls, including least privilege, multi-factor authentication, continuous monitoring, system backups, incident response, encryption, access control, security awareness training, and network boundary protection. I also incorporated compliance requirements such as HIPAA, HITECH, and PCI-DSS.

